    "reason": "A token-preserving ROST build changed Dan Marino's stored Speed byte from 40 to 99, booted in Xenia, and loaded/rendered the edited player record without the former startup crash. The desktop editor therefore exposes semantic per-attribute replacement under a strict public 0..99 authoring limit. A source value of native 100 is still displayed exactly and can be reverted, but the product does not author new 100 values. The game has no numeric ratings screen, so the isolated on-field effect of each attribute remains a separate gameplay-validation question."
